<title>Data Revenue =E2=80=94 Two Options =E2=80=94 Minds &amp; Models</tit=
le>


<div class=3D"wrap">
  <header>
    <div class=3D"eyebrow">Minds &amp; Models =C2=B7 Data business =C2=B7 R=
evenue model =E2=80=94 rev 2</div>
    <h1>Two ways to run it: personalization + data, or data only</h1>
    <p class=3D"kicker">Same sensor deployment from the finance plan, but n=
ow assuming <b>data rights are solved with every retailer</b> and rollout r=
uns as <b>3 chains in parallel</b>. The question this answers: keep persona=
lization and add data on top, or drop personalization and become a pure dat=
a-infrastructure business =E2=80=94 and what each does to revenue.</p>
    <div class=3D"meta">
      <span><b>Driver</b> Active Screens (sensors) from finance plan</span>
      <span><b>Density</b> 1,75 sensors/loc =C2=B7 125 loc/retailer</span>
      <span><b>Data figures</b> M&amp;M net of ~28% retailer rev-share</spa=
n>
    </div>
    <hr class=3D"rule">
  </header>

  <div class=3D"verdict">
    <div class=3D"l">The answer in one paragraph</div>
    <p><b>Option 1 (personalization + data)</b> is the bigger near-term top=
 line: ~=E2=82=AC10,6M M&amp;M revenue by 2031, because you keep the =E2=82=
=AC6,6M personalization line and stack ~=E2=82=AC4M of data net on top. <b>=
Option 2 (pure data)</b> is smaller in revenue =E2=80=94 ~=E2=82=AC4M base,=
 ~=E2=82=AC7,9M if data monetizes aggressively =E2=80=94 because you give u=
p personalization and share ~28% of data revenue with retailers. But Option=
 2 is the <b>leaner, more scalable, higher-multiple</b> business: at measur=
ement-currency valuations (8=E2=80=9315=C3=97 vs 4=E2=80=936=C3=97 for a mi=
xed SaaS), the aggressive pure-data case is worth <b>more equity value at h=
alf the revenue</b>. Option 1 maximizes revenue; Option 2 maximizes what th=
e revenue is worth =E2=80=94 and matches your original "in-store data infra=
structure" thesis.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D WHAT CHANGED =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D -->
  <section>
    <div class=3D"eyebrow">01 =C2=B7 What changed since rev 1</div>
    <h2>Three inputs, rewritten</h2>
    <div class=3D"changed">
