      <li><b>Option 1 bets on execution certainty.</b> Two revenue lines, p=
ersonalization funds the rollout, ~=E2=82=AC10,6M by 2031. You almost certa=
inly get there. The ceiling is the valuation multiple =E2=80=94 a two-produ=
ct company doesn't get the data-currency premium.</li>
      <li><b>Option 2 bets on category creation.</b> You give up =E2=82=AC6=
,6M of safe personalization revenue and a chunk of data revenue to retailer=
s, to become a clean data-infrastructure company. It only wins if data mone=
tizes aggressively =E2=80=94 but if it does, it's worth roughly <b>2=C3=97 =
Option 1's equity value</b> and matches your original market thesis.</li>
      <li><b>The hidden dependency is deployment funding.</b> Option 1's pe=
rsonalization cash is what pays for the sensors in the ground. Option 2 mus=
t replace that with brand co-funding and investment before the sensor curve=
 =E2=80=94 and therefore this entire data-revenue timeline =E2=80=94 can ha=
ppen. Solve that and Option 2 is viable; leave it unsolved and the pure-dat=
a curve slides right by 6=E2=80=9312 months.</li>
      <li><b>They're not mutually exclusive in time.</b> The strongest play=
 may be <b>Option 1 now, Option 2 later</b>: use personalization to fund de=
ployment and prove the data product, then drop personalization and re-rate =
as a pure data-currency business once rights, POS and brand demand are lock=
ed. The revenue lines above are the same sensors either way.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class=3D"mine"><b>Caveats that bound all of this.</b> (1) Same sen=
sor curve is assumed for both options; in pure-data it depends on replaceme=
nt funding actually landing. (2) Per-location ARR rests on one verified com=
parable (=C3=9AZEI 3,7M CZK) + your PMI/Nestl=C3=A9 points =E2=80=94 widen =
the band before quoting externally. (3) Figures are year-end run-rate, net =
of ~28% retailer share; recognized revenue lags. (4) The 8 named chains are=
 monetized by ~2028 (~1 700 sensors); everything past that assumes new CZ c=
hains then Europe from ~2030 =E2=80=94 the CZ-only ceiling is ~29 chains. (=
5) Valuation multiples are illustrative, not quotes.</div>
  </section>

  <p class=3D"foot">Model driver: "Number of Active Screens" from Minds &am=
p; Models bottom-up finance plan (FS-Month, 2026=E2=80=932032). Assumptions=
: 1,75 sensors/location, ~150-store monetization sample/retailer, rights so=
lved with all retailers, pipeline-paced concurrent rollouts (8 named chains=
 deploying 2026=E2=80=9328, ~2=E2=80=933 rising to ~8), brand-sales convers=
ion 30=E2=86=92100% (2026=E2=80=9329), ~28% retailer data rev-share. Pricin=
g ladder and pivot mechanics from the data-infrastructure strategy report (=
with verified NielsenIQ / =C3=9AZEI / IAB benchmarks). All figures EUR, yea=
